RED: two source tests and the independent IR test reject scalar w operands
with E3021. Shared admission now includes only F32/F64 alongside the previously
approved integer/polynomial vector carriers. No new emitter/register allocator,
numeric conversion, implicit fenv reset or opaque-asm interpretation is added.
Default operands print vN, with explicit b/h/s/d/q views; fixed reference
assembly confirms this. Matching inputs require identical scalar type.

GREEN tailored tests:
- 51 CLI inline-assembly tests, including both scalar fixtures, pass.
- 11 independent EvoIR assembly tests pass; malformed type/bank/fenv/world
  mutations fail validation and exact text round trips retain all fields.
- 13 MIR inline-assembly tests pass, including Simd32 allocation mutations.
- Proof reconstruction rejects changed constraints and clobbers for vector,
  f32 and f64, with three accepted controls and six rejected forgeries.
- Both source interpreters retain E3021 for reached opaque assembly.
- General-registers-only retains E4002; f128, wrong GPR/view and float/double
  matching mismatches retain E3021.
- The 12-output f32/f64 asm.goto cases each force at least 12 actual spills;
  allocation is checked independently, and values survive both selected edges
  plus a subsequent caller-saved SIMD clobber. Host native fixture also passes.

Fixed native lane: evo-flight-lab:sealed, linux/arm64, no network, image digest
2c23684c9cc5ef5899073b59844fa47cc3c1d894f2316e21f25d5d85be5a10e2;
GCC 14.2.0-19 / Clang 19.1.7, glibc 2.41.
GCC14/Clang19 O0/O2 source controls all pass. Actual EvoCC O0/O2 assembly is
linked by each reference compiler at O0/O2: eight whole-fixture executions,
eight environment executions (58 checks each), sixteen separate-TU calls in
both directions all pass. Environment checks cover four modes, prior/sticky
flags, rint/ceil, invalid division, FPCR modification followed by strict C FP,
and exact signed-zero/subnormal/infinity/qNaN/sNaN transport without flags.
Each fixture uses the existing source profile (-std=gnu11; environment worker
also -frounding-math); reference builds disable contraction. Worker builds use
-DSCALAR_ASM_WORKER. No tolerance is applied to bit/status comparisons.

Original command replay: ceil, floor, rint, rintf, __math_oflow, __math_uflow,
frexp and scalbn all emit and assemble (8/8). Original source and semantic
flags are unchanged; unrelated command omissions remain reported. The four
original scalar-asm objects are linked to musl-scalar-assembly-driver.c using
GCC14/Clang19 O0/O2, -frounding-math -fno-builtin and -lm: four subject and four
reference-object executions each pass 56 value/status checks. The driver uses
glibc's fenv interface; this is not a full musl libc-test result.

